<title>USA: Beverly Enterprises Inc Q4 earnings summary.</title>
<headline>Beverly Enterprises Inc Q4 earnings summary.</headline>
<dateline>FORT SMITH, Ark. 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr     loss    $0.03	     loss $0.65</p>
<p> Net     loss    3,269	     loss 63,756</p>
<p> Revs		838,744		  811,615</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  98,341		   98,497</p>
<p>	  12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr	profit $0.50	     loss $0.16</p>
<p> Net	profit 50,300	    loss 8,123</p>
<p> Revs		3,281,028		3,242,781</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  99,646		   92,233</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Income from continuing operations for 1996 Q4 was $21,735,000 or $0.22 per share, excluding previously announced one-time increase in provision for income taxes of $23,278,000 or $0.23 per share related to the November 1996 sale of the MedView Services business unit, as well as an extraordinary net charge of $1,726,000 or $0.02 per share related to debt refinancings.</p>
<p>1995 Q4 results include write-offs totalling $112,654,000 for impaired assets and cost-reduction actions. Excluding these charges, Beverly earned $0.10 per share in 1995 Q4.</p>
</text>
